{"title":"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem Statement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#1._Angle_Chasing_and_Setup\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">1. Angle Chasing and Setup</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#2._Congruence_and_Trigonometric_Relations_on_\\triangle_BTC\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">2. Congruence and Trigonometric Relations on \\triangle BTC</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#3._Solving_for_TB_+_TC\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">3. Solving for TB + TC</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest angle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> divide the circumcircle of the triangle into two arcs.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> be an interior point of the arc between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> which does not contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.  The perpendicular bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> meet the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce4ae7913470106b2c65a7d861bed8140c8e71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, respectively.  The lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9b04270bc2252040311c5d93719a5098da0518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f59c142b5e210555a9f93973a8cdb233b859c74f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.  Show that.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8cac4bf2978da60711b44013a288275a827f6f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AU=TB+TC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:IMO1997_Problem2.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/cd/IMO1997_Problem2.jpg/750px-IMO1997_Problem2.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"750\" height=\"422\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/cd/IMO1997_Problem2.jpg/1125px-IMO1997_Problem2.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/c/cd/IMO1997_Problem2.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_Statement\">Problem Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest angle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> divide the circumcircle of the triangle into two arcs. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> be an interior point of the arc between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> which does not contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. The perpendicular bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> meet the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce4ae7913470106b2c65a7d861bed8140c8e71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. The lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9b04270bc2252040311c5d93719a5098da0518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f59c142b5e210555a9f93973a8cdb233b859c74f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/385b64bdedcb8756dd226e88bf7bbe245512cdcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AU = TB + TC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"1._Angle_Chasing_and_Setup\">1. Angle Chasing and Setup</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: 1. Angle Chasing and Setup\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersections of the perpendicular bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> with the circumcircle, respectively. \n</p><p>We define the angles in the configuration using Greek letters as follows:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06110ece4dc8b6565d7ee6adad8734a62b2f16b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ALD = \\tau$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the circumcenter (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d591c3074650a5eaad2d407da2f01e87a4896c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA = OB$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9b71e7166831c20f03fc3696dd37d5f1da0559.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DL$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, any point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9b71e7166831c20f03fc3696dd37d5f1da0559.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DL$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is equidistant from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/9555254118d3e8d15d6d125edc1daa4a1e756226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LA = LB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />. With the shared side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/988eb7862af325a152533cff8375694dd9078fda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OL$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e977f1c07b8e85a9ed353676edbbc9669b3856c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BOL \\cong \\triangle OAL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" /> by SSS, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/143e29e018d3b5b94377ae528c4328b35fd2924f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OBL = \\angle BLO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"135\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c77b471ea93efb449e63aaa397645c1a69e769a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OUM = \\angle OMU = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"182\" height=\"14\" />. (Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is used here to replace the original <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> notation to avoid confusion with the geometric constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />).</li>\n<li>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa7583a1716b7dd99b154911fea1a9748f7999c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ODM = \\angle OMD = \\rho$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />.</li>\n<li>Let the base angle of the isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/545fbc70a68b6f88792f3491b69ded339b997cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AOU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>From the properties of the circumcircle:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1ef53d9b0f353908e9af59dd5cd181b4f02aa44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ZOD = 2\\rho$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a7a5cce5c8e1f831b4a9952bdafcaa5ecf46b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ZOU = 2\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /></dd>\n<dd>The vertex angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/c/aecae6be8fbe31485309afba8a2655c051780c96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle UOA = 2\\tau + 2\\rho + 2\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/545fbc70a68b6f88792f3491b69ded339b997cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AOU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />, the sum of angles gives the relation:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7c0d5d2636791f12d375fa57270bdc2a946052a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(\\lambda + \\rho + \\theta) + 2u = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>By the Law of Sines, the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce4ae7913470106b2c65a7d861bed8140c8e71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/7504d2ef2491ae427a7d36bc4cdc042df1bbce53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AU = 2R\\sin(\\theta + \\lambda + \\rho) = 2R\\cos u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"278\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<h4><span id=\"2._Congruence_and_Trigonometric_Relations_on_.5Ctriangle_BTC\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2._Congruence_and_Trigonometric_Relations_on_\\triangle_BTC\">2. Congruence and Trigonometric Relations on \\triangle BTC</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: 2. Congruence and Trigonometric Relations on \\triangle BTC\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38a4886fa3f4916ff63dbd2c3ca5d3b97166736f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG = GB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d1ae7e30b3abfd30c7173baa0754d4ad865efaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AGV = \\angle GVB = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" />. With the shared side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d12392e439f0bbe9572f4711855e03b76b594f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db2bf92344c26d957322ead14e55f88b7b4a465e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AGV \\cong \\triangle GVB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" /> by SAS, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19bda79287d63fe24c5ef5e4c87f23932a301cce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GBV = \\angle GAV = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"174\" height=\"14\" />. Furthermore, by accounting for the base angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37398752a756f923314a59363899ebe8a3f3e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />, this establishes that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/b/f5bfd83a04a9f07a2b7d1b4e932fa578526c0149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle VBO = \\angle VAO = u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"173\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>Similarly, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b37e78630de967d4d59bee4f809df21844340b64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AW = WC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbbdc4b83b4c947098e1137d39af9df0aa53fbaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA = OC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b586474708b6bf416d70dec9f2a20c30fe367c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OW$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> is a shared side, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe0252bae985ec2f47b6d8334ec874accd831df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AWO \\cong \\triangle WOC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" /> by SSS, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/021ab64298a6b73a7e42b23cb876b7abd77de67a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle WAO = \\angle WCO = u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"182\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08fa4eb17e2bc26565807238f06c3bbe871f4b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\xi = \\angle HCB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/41752e67cd033c961edd7532c9376bc82296d255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BOC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, we establish <b>Equation 1</b>:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee6ca0ee27be736496bbdf74f6ade98ee26d5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau + \\gamma = u + \\alpha + \\xi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f402cbc9b31330a0df4a48bf9fef1684d756bad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\xi = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />, we obtain:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faa2059e2fa69c952a49d2e602f88d035c5ee400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(u + A) = \\frac{BC}{2R} \\quad \\text{--- (Eq 1.1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"242\" height=\"39\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Applying the projection law on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f15fd3d4b6b84f274c198ebbc221662108dbf6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BTC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, we get <b>Equation 2</b>:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a01f45a26c63c7630da4df7643d3949df7813665.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TB\\cos(u + \\tau + \\gamma) + TC\\cos(\\alpha + \\xi) = BC \\quad \\text{--- (Eq 2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"419\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Substituting <b>Equation 1</b> into <b>Equation 2</b>:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6dcfcaf354e6a1245f8a2ab8fde7146e92da71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TB\\cos(2u + A) + TC\\cos A = BC \\quad \\text{--- (Eq 3)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"359\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>By the Law of Sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f15fd3d4b6b84f274c198ebbc221662108dbf6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BTC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, we have <b>Equation 4</b>:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7bb4876b84fc93a5f21f9bff4fc24b66920ff3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TB\\sin(2u + A) = TC\\sin A \\quad \\text{--- (Eq 4)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"304\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<h4><span id=\"3._Solving_for_TB_.2B_TC\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"3._Solving_for_TB_+_TC\">3. Solving for TB + TC</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: 3. Solving for TB + TC\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>From <b>Equation 4</b>, we express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c24f95fda0ea2207182fc089fbe14b6750570e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TB$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff4e3496c035136863c754c524957a29e7ff9b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TC$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd903da79b5768186e6736bc0816fd082076138.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TB = \\frac{TC\\sin A}{\\sin(2u + A)} \\quad \\text{--- (Eq 4.1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"248\" height=\"44\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Substituting (Eq 4.1) back into <b>Equation 3</b>:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9badf22840139fbe78a1dcb1c844f002d6ad659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{TC\\sin A \\cos(2u + A)}{\\sin(2u + A)}\\right) + TC\\cos A = BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"345\" height=\"45\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Multiplying the entire equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/930a64590e4fccd30bb1f3ad2aed92b97ac9a4aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(2u + A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" /> and applying the sine addition formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/3031b971a9325bbec4459125c08f9ba2506f6f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(X+Y) = \\sin X \\cos Y + \\cos X \\sin Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"312\" height=\"20\" />:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/b/29b65717afb81d7c2ac74cee19d61c8327de0222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TC\\sin(2u + 2A) = BC\\sin(2u + A) \\quad \\text{--- (Eq 4.1.1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"393\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>In a similar manner, solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff4e3496c035136863c754c524957a29e7ff9b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TC$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c24f95fda0ea2207182fc089fbe14b6750570e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TB$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> yields:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a0009910659eac2fddc477f356751dbeda8d882b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TB\\sin(2u + 2A) = BC\\sin A \\quad \\text{--- (Eq 4.2.1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Adding <b>Equation 4.1.1</b> and <b>Equation 4.2.1</b> together:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f55b02f1a7079dcbd8a7e9c3cfbbe5f39fe8a8fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(TC + TB)\\sin(2u + 2A) = BC\\left(\\sin(2u + A) + \\sin A\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"421\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Applying the sum-to-product identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a140834d510cf25a1ca3deee481b583693e5093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin X + \\sin Y = 2\\sin\\frac{X+Y}{2}\\cos\\frac{X-Y}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"313\" height=\"39\" /> on the right-hand side:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/402e6220926548c5e3ea7b34626e456da345d02a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(TC + TB)\\cdot 2\\sin(u + A)\\cos(u + A) = 2BC\\sin(u + A)\\cos u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"478\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42fa9fb84d3b46707129c67cbe616a67734c20bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sin(u + A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76cd7fcfb1a7059e4f6f9289c0c456b8800c1816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(u+A) \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />):\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb49f319b1d1f0c90ed59a0ddc5c97367750afcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(TC + TB)\\cos(u + A) = BC\\cos u \\quad \\text{--- (Eq 5)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"361\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Finally, substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/5/6e5d2c1b830fdbffd0060ac591832932d195cdf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 2R\\cos(u + A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> from <b>Equation 1.1</b> into <b>Equation 5</b>:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26a01828de1bd41ea6a316c4e2a77d8ba8876601.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(TC + TB)\\cos(u + A) = 2R\\cos(u + A)\\cos u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"357\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/0/e209ab59668ced5753dffeedaacb277f1ddd193f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(u + A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />, we get:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c919d5630ff199839cdf5f482a5b26dca1f05421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TC + TB = 2R\\cos u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Since we previously established that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a0d607bf19fde92f8bda0e10b2ec25c1572868c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AU = 2R\\cos u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />, we successfully complete the proof:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/d/61d75c6ce93cff337375cddd3fe2cbfa14deb4ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AU = TB + TC \\quad \\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"16\" /></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO\" title=\"1997 IMO\">1997 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190616\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 621/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20691/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.721      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.721      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25395:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190616 and revision id 285319. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}